# Build artifacts
# Anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `assets/` matched every directory of
# that name at any depth — including `carrot/web/assets/`, which holds the
# logo and the nine font files the stylesheet loads. They were never
# committed, so a fresh clone 404s all ten and the whole typography system
# falls back to system fonts while the brand mark renders as an empty box.
/assets/
dist/
gui/dist/
gui/node_modules/
# The other node_modules. `gui/` was ignored from the start and this one never
# was, so 8,387 files of esbuild and Monaco sources were committed — a clone
# that downloads a compiler to serve a bundle it already has. The bundles
# themselves stay tracked (carrot/web/vendor), because those are what makes a
# checkout run offline; this is only the machinery that produced them, and
# `npm install` in webvendor/ brings it back.
webvendor/node_modules/
*.egg-info/
build/carrot/_build.py
.pytest_cache/

# Editor and agent scratch. None of it is Carrot; all of it was committed.
# .qoder alone carried 105 files, including a dozen screenshots of the UI
# mid-verification that describe a version of the app that no longer exists.
.claude/
.qoder/
_ui_check*.png
